n-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Bulten</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Shirango</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Melchers</surname><given-names>WJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Massuger</surname><given-names>LF</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2008</year><article-title>Biological behavior of CIN lesions is predictable by multiple parameter logistic regression models.</article-title><source>Carcinogenesis</source><volume>29</volume><fpage>840</fpage><lpage>845</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">18310095</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0004958-Srinivasan1"><label>18</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Srinivasan</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Sedmak</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Jewell</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name></person-group><year>2002</year><article-title>Effect of fixatives and tissue processing on the content and integrity of nucleic acids.</article-title><source>Am J Pathol</source><volume>161</volume><fpage>1961</fpage><lpage>1971</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12466110</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0004958-Hayat1"><label>19</label><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Hayat</surname><given-names>MA</given-names></name></person-group><year>1989</year><source>Principles and techniques of electron microscopy: Biological applications</source><publisher-loc>London</publisher-loc><publisher-name>MacMillan Press</publisher-name><fpage>38, 92, 401</fpage><lpage>403</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0004958-VanHamont2"><label>20</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Van Hamont</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Bekkers</surname><given-names>RL</given-names></name><name><surname>Massuger</surname><give